    {
      "id": "l1",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Why 3–10 years is a different game",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Why 3–10 years is a different game"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/1-dlaczego-3-10-lat-to-inna-gr.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "You have time to **ride out some of the drops**, but not enough to ignore every crash. That's why you combine different assets:"
            },
            {
              "type": "list",
              "items": [
                "**Stocks** – bring growth",
                "**Bonds** – bring stability"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "The goal: **beat inflation** without the risk of losing half just before you withdraw."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l2",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Setting a goal and an amount",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Setting a goal and an amount"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/2-wyznaczanie-celu-i-kwoty.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A good goal has **an amount and a date**. Instead of “I want to save” – “**20,000 € for a down payment in 6 years**”."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Then you can easily work out **how much to put aside** each month and what risk you can take."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "The closer the goal date, the more money you move into **safer assets**."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
    {
      "id": "l3",
      "kind": "lesson",
      "title": "Why not put everything on one card",
      "pages": [
        {
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "Why not put everything on one card"
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "image": "obrazki/3-nie-wszystko-na-jedna-karte.png",
              "width": 1,
              "maxHeight": 240,
              "caption": ""
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "When all your capital sits in one asset, **one bad year** can destroy the plan."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Splitting into **stocks, bonds and cash** means that when one part falls, the others usually hold their value or rise."
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "text": "The portfolio grows more slowly in the best case, but **hurts much less** in the worst."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "minigame": {
        "game": "",
        "settings": []
      },
      "tasks": []
    },
